From cfac4382f2d356ed88bf984865dbfeb85c488dbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:47:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Capture: phone page, free Gemini backend, validated
 fields, accuracy eval

- GET /capture/ui, GET /capture/items, POST /capture/tasks/done: see what was
  captured and tick tasks off. Token check moved to a module with no upstream
  imports so it is tested directly.
- Sorting runs on Claude or on Gemini's free tier (CAPTURE_BACKEND, auto picks
  Claude when its key is set). The response names the model in sorted_by.
- Model output is validated before it is written: topic must be configured,
  due must be a date and only on tasks, currency must be a code, amount must be
  finite and not negative, expense text is spreadsheet-formula safe.
- Prompt tightened on quoted prices, commitment, due dates, empty answers and
  topics; topics can carry a description.
- CAPTURE_TZ, one retry and a 45 s limit, short error reasons, a readable phone
  message when transcription fails.
- /ask on Claude is its own opt-in (ASK_BACKEND=claude): /ask has no token.
- .env.example token line no longer carries an inline comment; token is
  stripped. uv.lock now includes anthropic.
- evals/: 59 cases, scorer, runner. Measured on gemini-3.1-flash-lite: 57/59.
