+## See it and tick it off
+
+Open `https://<your-server>/capture/ui` on the phone and add it to the Home Screen. It
+asks for `CAPTURE_TOKEN` once and keeps it in that browser (localStorage); "Forget token"
+removes it. Four tabs: Tasks, Notes, Expenses, Inbox, newest first. Tap a checkbox to tick
+a task; open "Done" and tap again to reopen it. Expenses shows one total per currency.
+
+The page is one HTML file with no data in it, so it is served without the token. Every
+data call it makes sends `Authorization: Bearer <CAPTURE_TOKEN>`. Use HTTPS (Tailscale):
+over plain HTTP the token crosses the network in the clear.
+
+| Route | Token | Does |
+|---|---|---|
+| `GET /capture/ui` | no | The page. |
+| `GET /capture/items` | yes | Everything in `tasks.md`, `notes.md`, `expenses.csv`, `inbox.md` as JSON. |
+| `POST /capture/tasks/done` | yes | Body `{"id": "<task id>", "done": true}`. `false` reopens. |
+
+```bash
+curl -s http://localhost:8000/capture/items -H "Authorization: Bearer $CAPTURE_TOKEN"
+```
+
+```json
+{
+  "tasks": {
+    "open": [{"id": "3f0c9a1b2d4e5f60", "text": "Collect the bike", "due": "2026-11-14", "topic": "motorcycle", "done": false}],
+    "done": []
+  },
+  "notes": [{"at": "2026-11-12 14:03", "text": "Lorry quote was 1,200", "topic": "move"}],
+  "expenses": {
+    "items": [{"at": "2026-11-12T14:03:00", "amount": 500.0, "currency": "MYR", "text": "Deposit for the bike", "topic": "motorcycle"}],
+    "totals": {"MYR": 500.0}
+  },
+  "inbox": [{"at": "2026-11-13 10:00", "text": "call the landlord", "error": "Claude rate limit"}],
+  "skipped": {"tasks": 0, "notes": 0, "expenses": 0, "inbox": 0}
+}
+```
+
+You can still edit the files by hand. What to expect:
+
+- A task's `id` is made from its text, not its line number. Edit or delete a task and its
+  old id stops working: a tick sent from a page that has not reloaded gets 404 and changes
+  nothing. Ticking a task that is already ticked gets 409. The page reloads the list itself.
+- A tick rewrites `tasks.md` through a temp file and a rename, and changes only the one
+  character inside the brackets. If the file was saved by something else in that moment
+  the tick is refused (409) and the other save is kept.
+- A line the server cannot read (a task with no `- [ ]`, an expense whose amount is not a
+  number) is left alone in the file, not shown, and counted in `skipped`. The page says so
+  under the list. A hand-written `- some note` with no timestamp is shown.
+- An expense with no currency is totalled under `?`. One with no amount is listed but not
+  totalled.
