+`POST /ask` (and the bundled ASR-Ask Shortcut) stays on Gemini unless you set
+`ASK_BACKEND=claude`. It is a separate switch on purpose: `/ask` has no token, so with
+Claude behind it anyone who can reach the server can spend your Anthropic key. `/status`
+still reports it under the `gemini` key, because the PWA reads that name; the `model` value
+there shows which one is live.
+
+## Checking accuracy
+
+`evals/` holds 59 dictated-note cases (Manglish, misheard words, relative dates, quoted but
+unpaid prices) and a scorer. Run it against the real model:
+
+```bash
+GEMINI_API_KEY=... uv run python evals/run_eval.py --backend gemini --concurrency 1 --delay 4.5
+ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=... uv run python evals/run_eval.py --backend claude
+```
+
+See `evals/README.md` for what the numbers mean and their limits.
+
+## Docker
+
+`docker-compose.yml` is not set up for capture: it passes none of the variables above and
+keeps `DATA_DIR` inside the container, so a rebuild would delete your files. Run from a
+checkout (`make dev`, launchd or systemd) until you add the variables and a data volume.
 
 ## Settings
 
 | Variable | Default | Meaning |
 |---|---|---|
-| `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | none | Claude key. Unset means captures go to the inbox and `/ask` stays on Gemini. |
+| `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | none | Claude key. When set, Claude sorts captures. |
+| `GEMINI_API_KEY` | none | Gemini key. Sorts captures when no Claude key is set. With neither, captures go to the inbox. |
+| `CAPTURE_BACKEND` | `auto` | `claude`, `gemini`, or `auto` (Claude if its key is set, else Gemini). |
+| `ASK_BACKEND` | `gemini` | Set to `claude` to answer `/ask` with Claude. `/ask` has no token. |
 | `CLAUDE_MODEL` | `claude-opus-5-5` | Model for `/ask`. |
 | `CLAUDE_SYSTEM_PROMPT` | short voice-assistant persona | System prompt for `/ask`. |
 | `CAPTURE_TOKEN` | none | Bearer token the Shortcut sends. Unset means 503. |
-| `CAPTURE_MODEL` | `claude-opus-5-5` | Any Claude model id. |
-| `CAPTURE_TOPICS` | empty | Comma-separated tags Claude may attach. |
+| `CAPTURE_MODEL` | `claude-opus-5-5` or `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` | Model id for the backend in use. |
+| `CAPTURE_TOPICS` | empty | Comma-separated `tag` or `tag: description`. |
+| `CAPTURE_TZ` | server clock | IANA zone, for example `Asia/Kuala_Lumpur`. |
